# Canonical reviewed solution: directly authored binary, not assembler output.
11111010 # instruction | CLI | Keep interrupts masked while using the stack.
10111100 00000000 01111100 # instruction | MOV SP,7C00 | Set a known empty stack.
10111000 00010001 00010001 # instruction | MOV AX,1111 | First value to push.
10111011 00100010 00100010 # instruction | MOV BX,2222 | Second value to push.
10111001 00000000 00000000 # instruction | MOV CX,0 | Initialize the first requested result.
10111010 00000000 00000000 # instruction | MOV DX,0 | Initialize the second requested result.
01010000 # instruction | PUSH AX | Push 1111 first, storing it below the initial SP.
01010011 # instruction | PUSH BX | Push 2222 last, so it must be popped first.
01011001 # instruction | POP CX | CX receives the most recently pushed word, 2222.
01011010 # instruction | POP DX | DX receives the earlier word, 1111; SP is balanced.
11110100 # instruction | HLT | Stop after the last-in-first-out transfer.
